#
# Written by openshift-4-cluster/tasks/prepare-host.yml because this host has
# an IPv6 default route whose gateway does not answer. See that file, and
# docs/preparing-the-host.md, for the measurements that motivated it.
#
# glibc discards its entire built-in policy table as soon as a single
# precedence line is present, so the whole default table has to be restated
# here rather than adding one line. The table below is the RFC 6724 default
# (glibc has implemented RFC 6724 rather than the older RFC 3484 since 2.17,
# and every currently supported RHEL/CentOS/Rocky/Debian ships a newer glibc
# than that), with exactly one value changed: ::ffff:0:0/96 is raised from 35
# to 100 so getaddrinfo() returns IPv4 ahead of IPv6.
#
# Restating the older RFC 3484 table here would be a bug: it omits the ULA
# (fc00::/7), Teredo (2001::/32), site-local and 6bone entries, so those
# addresses would fall through to the ::/0 catch-all at precedence 40 instead
# of being correctly deprioritised.
#
# This does not disable IPv6. If the gateway starts answering, remove this
# file (or set prefer_ipv4_when_ipv6_gateway_dead: false and re-run
# 01-prepare-host.yml) and normal RFC 6724 ordering returns.

label ::1/128        0
label ::/0           1
label 2002::/16      2
label ::/96          3
label ::ffff:0:0/96  4
label 2001:0::/32    5
label fc00::/7      13
label fec0::/10     11
label 3ffe::/16     12

precedence ::1/128       50
precedence ::/0          40
precedence ::ffff:0:0/96 100
precedence 2002::/16     30
precedence 2001:0::/32    5
precedence fc00::/7       3
precedence ::/96          1
precedence fec0::/10      1
precedence 3ffe::/16      1
